          "filename": "Canfea - geograph.org.uk - 268121.jpg",
          "caption": "Canfea This view was taken looking from the track to the Ardgroom Stone Circle across the townland of Canfea. Keecragh Mountain, with its twin peaks of 363 and 343 metres, is the distant hill in V7356 The tiny dark specks on the electricity cables in front of the hill are rows of starlings perched at precisely the same distance from one another. When one new one arrived to perch in the centre of the flock all the others had to shuffle away to maintain their distance from their neighbours.",
